@tobiasdiez I'm not exactly sure how this would have been possible here. For some sub-test sure, but would it have been possible to make nested loops where I test all java8 versions against all java9 version when I provide them as parameter test? Yes, I think that is possible. The junit 5 documentation contains the code
````java
@ParameterizedTest
@MethodSource("stringAndIntProvider")
void testWithMultiArgMethodSource(String first, int second) {
    assertNotNull(first);
    assertNotEquals(0, second);
}

static Stream<Arguments> stringAndIntProvider() {
    return Stream.of(Arguments.of("foo", 1), Arguments.of("bar", 2));
}
````
By changing `stringAndIntProvider` you can generate every possible combination of java 8 and java 9 version strings. Anyway, no need to change it for this PR. Was just a remark for the next time.
