Fixed imports issue. Please reviewThanks for your contribution. With your changes, the value of the field in the crossreferenced entry is always taken, even if it specified in the entry itself. This is not the problem descried in #5045 and not according to the biblatex specification. 

The real problem is that biblatex specifies a more complex crossref resolution. I think a proper fix should go along the following lines:
```java
if (!result.isPresent() && (database != null)) {
            Optional<BibEntry> referred = database.getReferencedEntry(this);
            if (!referred.isEmpty()) {
                  result = referred.get()..getFieldOrAlias(field);
                  if (result.isEmpty()) {
                       if (type == InProceedings && field = FieldNames.booktitle) {
