@Siedlerchr had the impression that JabRef was slower (see https://github.com/koppor/jabref/issues/440#issuecomment-757376716). Do we need to test it? I no longer have the impression. 6.8 seems fast again with jabref or it was another bug fix- `jabref.bat -n -h` works (besides the strange output https://github.com/koppor/jabref/issues/486)
- Did not see performance issues during runtime

Thus, I'll go ahead with merging. We can revert if some developers experience issues.
